.TH UWG 8 "2026-11-16" "UmbraWG" "System Administration"

.SH NAME
uwg \- set and retrieve configuration of UmbraWG interfaces

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uwg
[\fICOMMAND\fP] [\fIOPTIONS\fP]... [\fIARGS\fP]...

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B uwg
is the configuration utility for UmbraWG tunnel interfaces. The interfaces
themselves are created and removed with
.BR ip-link (8);
addresses and routes are configured with
.BR ip-address (8)
and
.BR ip-route (8).
.B uwg
changes only UmbraWG-specific settings.

The utility talks to the
.B umbrawg
kernel module over generic netlink. When the interface is served by the
userspace
.B umbrawg
daemon, it uses the UAPI socket
.IR /var/run/umbrawg/<interface>.sock
instead. The transport is selected automatically.

If no \fICOMMAND\fP is given, \fBshow\fP is assumed.

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBshow\fP {\fI<interface>\fP | \fIall\fP | \fIinterfaces\fP} [\fIPARAMETER\fP]
Shows the configuration and runtime state. With \fIinterfaces\fP, prints the
names of all UmbraWG interfaces separated by spaces. With a \fIPARAMETER\fP,
prints one tab-separated value per line, intended for scripts. With
\fIall\fP and a \fIPARAMETER\fP, every line is prefixed with the interface name.
.PP
\fIPARAMETER\fP is one of:
\fIpublic-key\fP, \fIprivate-key\fP, \fIlisten-port\fP, \fIfwmark\fP,
\fIpeers\fP, \fIpreshared-keys\fP, \fIendpoints\fP, \fIallowed-ips\fP,
\fIlatest-handshakes\fP, \fIpersistent-keepalive\fP, \fItransfer\fP,
\fIdump\fP, \fIjc\fP, \fIjmin\fP, \fIjmax\fP, \fIs1\fP, \fIs2\fP, \fIs3\fP,
\fIs4\fP, \fIh1\fP, \fIh2\fP, \fIh3\fP, \fIh4\fP, \fIi1\fP, \fIi2\fP,
\fIi3\fP, \fIi4\fP, \fIi5\fP, \fIheader-protection-key\fP,
\fIcontent-padding-addition\fP, \fIrekey-after-time\fP, \fIrekey-timeout\fP,
\fIreject-after-time\fP, \fIkeepalive-timeout\fP,
\fImax-handshake-attempts\fP, \fIrandom-trailers\fP, \fIdisable-cookies\fP,
\fIadvanced-security\fP.
.TP
\fBshowconf\fP \fI<interface>\fP
Shows the current configuration in the format described by
\fICONFIGURATION FILE FORMAT\fP.
.TP
\fBset\fP \fI<interface>\fP [\fIARGUMENT\fP]...
Changes the configuration. Device arguments:
.RS
.TP
\fBlisten-port\fP \fI<port>\fP
UDP listen port; 0 or omission selects a random port.
.TP
\fBfwmark\fP \fI<mark>\fP
Firewall mark as a decimal value or \fB0x\fP-prefixed hexadecimal value.
.TP
\fBprivate-key\fP \fI<file>\fP
Reads the private key from a file. A device or empty file removes the key.
.TP
\fBjc\fP, \fBjmin\fP, \fBjmax\fP, \fBs1\fP, \fBs2\fP, \fBs3\fP, \fBs4\fP \fI<value>\fP
Obfuscation parameters from 0 to 65535.
.TP
\fBh1\fP, \fBh2\fP, \fBh3\fP, \fBh4\fP \fI<value>\fP[\fB-\fP\fI<value>\fP]
Magic header value or inclusive range of 32-bit values.
.TP
\fBi1\fP, \fBi2\fP, \fIi3\fP, \fIi4\fP, \fIi5\fP \fI<descriptor>\fP
Intermediate header descriptor.
.TP
\fBheader-protection-key\fP \fI<file>\fP
Reads the 32-byte header protection key from a file.
.TP
\fBcontent-padding-addition\fP, \fBrekey-after-time\fP, \fBrekey-timeout\fP,
\fBreject-after-time\fP, \fBkeepalive-timeout\fP, \fBmax-handshake-attempts\fP \fI<value>\fP[\fB-\fP\fI<value>\fP]
Numeric parameter or inclusive 16-bit range.
.TP
\fBrandom-trailers\fP, \fBdisable-cookies\fP \fI<on|off>\fP
Boolean UmbraWG 3.1 parameters.
.RE
.IP
Peer arguments are introduced by \fBpeer\fP \fI<base64-public-key>\fP and accept
\fBremove\fP, \fBpreshared-key\fP \fI<file>\fP, \fBendpoint\fP
\fI<address>:<port>\fP, \fBpersistent-keepalive\fP \fI<value>\fP, and
\fBallowed-ips\fP \fI<cidr>[,<cidr>]...\fP. Repeating \fBpeer\fP starts a new
peer. An empty \fBallowed-ips\fP value removes all allowed IPs.
.TP
\fBsetconf\fP \fI<interface>\fP \fI<file>\fP
Applies a configuration file. Existing peers not present in the file are
removed.
.TP
\fBaddconf\fP \fI<interface>\fP \fI<file>\fP
Appends a configuration file. Peers already present on the interface are kept
and updated, and peers absent from the file are not removed.
.TP
\fBsyncconf\fP \fI<interface>\fP \fI<file>\fP
Synchronizes the interface with a configuration file: peers that are missing
from the file are removed explicitly, while unchanged peers keep their active
sessions.
.TP
\fBversion\fP
Prints the program name and version.
.TP
\fBhelp\fP
Prints usage information.
.TP
\fBgenkey\fP
Generates a private key and writes it to standard output.
.TP
\fBgenpsk\fP
Generates a preshared key and writes it to standard output.
.TP
\fBpubkey\fP
Reads a private key from standard input and writes the public key to standard
output.

.SH CONFIGURATION FILE FORMAT
The file is INI-like and case-insensitive. Comments start with \fB#\fP.
The \fB[Interface]\fP section accepts:
.PP
\fBPrivateKey\fP, \fBListenPort\fP, \fBFwMark\fP, \fBJc\fP, \fBJmin\fP,
\fBJmax\fP, \fBS1\fP, \fBS2\fP, \fBS3\fP, \fBS4\fP, \fBH1\fP, \fBH2\fP,
\fBH3\fP, \fBH4\fP, \fBI1\fP, \fBI2\fP, \fBI3\fP, \fBI4\fP, \fBI5\fP,
\fBHeaderProtectionKey\fP, \fBContentPaddingAddition\fP,
\fBRekeyAfterTime\fP, \fBRekeyTimeout\fP, \fBRejectAfterTime\fP,
\fBKeepaliveTimeout\fP, \fBMaxHandshakeAttempts\fP, \fBRandomTrailers\fP,
\fBDisableCookies\fP.
.PP
Each \fB[Peer]\fP section accepts \fBPublicKey\fP, \fBPresharedKey\fP,
\fBAllowedIPs\fP, \fBEndpoint\fP, and \fBPersistentKeepalive\fP.
.PP
The \fBuwg-quick\fP-only keys \fBAddress\fP, \fBDNS\fP, \fBMTU\fP, \fBTable\fP,
\fBPreUp\fP, \fBPostUp\fP, \fBPreDown\fP, \fBPostDown\fP, and \fBSaveConfig\fP
are rejected by \fBuwg\fP and are documented in
.BR uwg-quick (8).

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WG_COLOR_MODE
\fBalways\fP or \fBnever\fP; otherwise color is enabled only on a terminal.
.TP
.B WG_HIDE_KEYS
When set to \fBnever\fP, private and preshared keys are printed in
\fBshow\fP output; by default they are hidden.
.TP
.B UWG_RUNTIME_DIR
Directory containing userspace UAPI sockets. Defaults to
.IR /var/run/umbrawg .

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/umbrawg/*.conf
Configuration files used by
.BR uwg-quick (8).
.TP
.I /var/run/umbrawg/*.sock
UAPI sockets of the userspace daemon.

.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success, non-zero on error. Errors are written to standard error.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR uwg-quick (8),
.BR ip-link (8),
.BR ip-address (8),
.BR ip-route (8)
